! ax5b_160_test1c_mask.strap -- jb_ax5b "I-BOX 5", routine 1260
! ("----1260---CHECK MASK, INDICATOR, AND INTERRUPT.", banner PDF p.8),
! its TEST 1C: IBM's test that the PROGRAMMABLE bits of the MASK
! REGISTER, 20-47, can each be set to one and to zero.
!
!   PDF p.14     014253.40-014272.00  I6011: bits 20-24 (value field)
!   PDF pp.14-15 014272.40-014316.00  I60B3: its error table, 10 entries
!   PDF p.15     014316.40-014337.00  I6016: bits 46-47 (refill field)
!   PDF p.16     014337.40-014347.00  I60B4: its error table, 4 entries
!   PDF p.16     014347.40-014371.00  I6021: bits 28-45 (count field)
!   PDF pp.17-19 014371.40-014501.00  I60B5: its error table, 36 entries
!   PDF p.20     014501.40-014536.40  I6027: bit 25 (flag), 26-27 (spare)
!   PDF p.21     014537.00-014555.40  I6031: bit 26, the exit (B,SSW),
!                                     continuity BIT2
!   PDF p.86     023042.00-023045.40, 023060.00, 023301.00: I60K1-I60K4,
!                                     I60K15 and I60DMP, as printed
!   PDF pp.114-115 024501.00-024621.00: the constant pool and BIT0-BIT63,
!                                     as decks/ax5b_bit_table.strap
!                                     transcribes them (verified there)
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi; every CODE row
! (I6011-I6015 on p.14, I6016-I6020 on p.15, I60B4 and I6021-I6026 on
! p.16, all of pp.20-21) read again at 400 dpi, and every row agreed.
! The error-table rows (pp.14-19) were read at 150 dpi; they repeat one
! printed pattern.  Checked row for row
! against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax5b_160_test1c_mask_listing.py (382 rows, 28 symbols).
!
! THE RULE.  Reference Manual Figure 11, the Indicator List (printed
! p.43, PDF p.46): the "Mask" column prints "m" (settable) for
! indicators 20-47; printed p.48 (PDF p.51), "Mask Register": "Those
! corresponding to indicators 20-47 can be set to 0 or 1 by program
! control."  The model has it in bsv/StretchStorage.bsv's addrMask write
! ("{20'hFFFFF, v[43:16], 16'h0000}").  TEST 1A/1B
! (decks/ax5b_160_test1ab_mask.strap) checked the FIXED bits; this is
! the settable half, and it checks each settable bit by itself, to one
! and to zero.
!
! ENTRY STATE.  IBM reaches I6011 by TEST 1B's "BD,$+.32" (014251.40), so
! TEST 1C runs with the interruption system DISABLED; the model resets
! disabled (StretchStorage.bsv's irqEn, mkConfigReg(False)), so a run
! from END starts in the same state.  Disabled, no mask bit can cause an
! interruption (printed p.48: "interruption requires the mask bit to be
! 1, the indicator bit to be 1, and the mechanism to be enabled").
!
! HOW TEST 1C WORKS.  The mask is word 12; TI moves it to and from an
! index register, so each group of bits is read through the index-word
! field it lands in (Reference Manual printed pp.24-25, PDF pp.27-28):
!   * 20-24, the VALUE field (I6012, five passes).  Z,12.0 clears the
!     mask, TI loads BITk, and KV compares the mask's bits 0-24
!     algebraically with BITk + I60K1 (bits 0-19 ones).  For bit 24, the
!     sign, "-SENSE BIT 24 SPECIAL CASE." (KCI,$X2,1.0 on the last
!     pass) loads I60K15 (-(777777.60)) instead.  Then Z,12.0 and the
!     mask read back must equal I60K1: the to-zero half.
!   * 46-47, the REFILL field (I6017, two passes).  SR,$X5,$X6 moves the
!     mask's refill (46-63) into a value, compared against BIT(k+1)'s
!     refill, which a self-planted LX (SVA,$X3,$+.32) loads.
!   * 28-45, the COUNT field (I6021, eighteen passes).  SC,$X1,I60DMP
!     moves the mask's count (28-45) into I60DMP's address part, which
!     must be above BIT(k+1)'s count.
!   * 25, the FLAG (I6027).  BXF on the read-back index word must take
!     with BIT25 in the mask, BZXF without it.
!   * 26-27, the two SPARE bits, by the routine's best trick: the mask
!     is loaded from an INSTRUCTION word (I60K2 SX / I60K3 C+I / I60K4
!     SV, each "$X1,I60DMP" plus NOP, p.86), read back, its value parts
!     replaced by the instruction's own (LV/SX/LV/SV), and the result,
!     planted at I6028/I6029/I6032, EXECUTED.  Bits 25-27 of that word
!     are op-code bits (SX prints "10", C+I "00", SV "30"), so they come
!     from the mask: a lost or spurious bit 26 or 27 turns the planted
!     SX/C+I/SV into one of the others, and what lands in I60DMP (all
!     ones, nothing, or a value with zero count) names the failure.
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: the model PASSES IBM's checks (PC 1410 = SSW,
! SEN 0) from END (I6011).  No disagreement with the listing.  Final
! state, pinned in run_tests.sh:
!   MASK (word 12) = 0xfffff33000000000: 0-19 ones plus 22, 23, 26, 27,
!     I60K4's bits, the last word loaded into it.
!   I60DMP (023301) = 0xffffff8000000000: what the planted SV,$X1,I60DMP
!     stored -- X1's value (all ones), bits 0-24, count untouched.
!   X0 = 0xffffff8000000000 (LX of I60DMP); X2 = 0x20000 (BIT46's
!   refill, value zeroed by SC); X3 = 0xa60800000000000, value 024602.00
!   = BIT48 (two passes past BIT46); X4 = 0x650600000000000, value
!   014501.40 = I60B5 + 18 x 4 words; X5 = 0xa60000000010000, value
!   024600.00 = BIT46, refill 0x10000 (mask bit 47, from I6018's TI);
!   X6 = 0x400000040000, value 1.00 = BIT45's count, count 1.
!   CYCLES 10326.
!   X values print the model's packIndexWord layout (bsv/StretchTypes.bsv):
!   value in bits 63-40, sign 39, flag 38, spare 37-36, count 35-18,
!   refill 17-0.  CYCLES is MODEL BEHAVIOUR.
!
! MODEL INJECTIONS, OBSERVED (a scratch copy of bsv/; the tracked bsv/
! never touched; StretchStorage.bsv's addrMask write each time):
!   M1 mask bit 30 (BSV 33) not settable: "{20'hFFFFF, v[43:34], 1'b0,
!     v[32:16], 16'h0000}" -> FAIL: PC 1416 (SERS), SEN 0x640a00000000000
!     (return 014402.40: the entry at 014401.40, "-MASK BIT 30 TO ONE
!     FAILURE."), X4 0x640600000400000 (value 014401.40, that entry;
!     count 16 passes left), I60DMP 0, MASK 0xfffff00000000000, X0 0, X2
!     0x1000000100000000, X5 0xa5c400000010000, X6 0x4000000400000000,
!     CYCLES 3410.  Only X3 passes.
!   M2 mask bit 26 (BSV 37) not settable: "{20'hFFFFF, v[43:38], 1'b0,
!     v[36:16], 16'h0000}" -> FAIL at the last check of all: PC 1416, SEN
!     0x65a000000000000 (return 014550.00: the SIC at 014547.00, "-MASK
!     REG BIT 26 TO ONE FAILURE."), MASK 0xfffff31000000000 (I60K4's bit
!     26 lost), I60DMP and X0 0xffffffffffffffff -- the planted SV,$X1 ran
!     as SX,$X1 and stored the whole index word, the trick above, seen --
!     CYCLES 10286.  X2-X6 pass (the 20-24, 28-47, 25 and I60K2/I60K3
!     checks never need bit 26 set).
!   CONTROL: the unmodified bsv/ in the same scratch copy, the same pins:
!     every pin passes (SEN, I60DMP, MASK, X0, X2-X6, PC 1410), CYCLES
!     10326.  StretchStorage.bsv restored from a saved copy between
!     injections; cmp IDENTICAL with the tracked file at the end.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points at the addresses jb_ax4b PDF p.193's SYN table
!     prints, which these pages' own machine code repeats (SSW 1301.0,
!     SERS 1304.0, SEN 1310.0, SENO 1311.0).  SSW is a PASS halt, SERS a
!     FAIL halt, SEN/SENO data words SIC stores into, as in
!     decks/ax5b_160_test1ab_mask.strap.  TEST 1C has no prologue of its
!     own (it is entered from I6010, TEST 1B's continuity block), so
!     RET/IDF1/DPET13 are not needed.
!   * IC260 (022737.00) is SYN'd at the address these pages' own machine
!     code prints for it ("LX,$X13,IC260" 22737.32 10).
!   * Only the p.86 rows TEST 1C reads are placed (I60K1-I60K4, I60K15,
!     I60DMP); I60K5-I60K14 and the rest of the pool are not, so the
!     words between are zero here.  decks/ax5b_160k_constants.strap has
!     023042.00-023070.00 in full.
!   * Notation only: "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")"; the label
!     glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I60.., I00O), as for
!     every ax5b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  p.16 prints
!     "LVI,$X5,BIT 28" with a space; written BIT28 (the printed address
!     24556.13 is BIT28's).

! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! ---- routine 1260's own label outside these pages, SYN'd at the
! address this listing prints for it (an input, not a witness) --------
IC260   SYN, (8)22737.0               ! -CONTINUITY REG 1260. (PDF p.83)
!
